nio: defer bsdinit_task to the init thread's AST

Run 605 fails with assert(task != kernel_task) in task_start_halt_locked:
calling bsdinit_task() on the boot thread means current_proc() is kernproc
and current_task() is kernel_task, so exec uses the wrong map/task and the
failure path tries to halt the kernel task (assert).  The map switch in
runs 603-605 could not fix this because the task itself is wrong.

Since run 598/602 the init thread is created successfully (post-cloneproc
is reached) and cloneproc returns, so let the normal bsd_ast() trigger
run bsdinit_task() on the real init thread, where current_proc/task/map
are all correct.  A panel mark confirms bsd_init no longer calls it
directly.  Diagnosis only.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index 03e112c..c4bb930 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -1271,14 +1271,14 @@ bsd_init(void)
 #endif /* DEVELOPMENT || DEBUG */
 
 	bsd_init_kprintf("done\n");
-	/* nio: bsdinit_task(), which execs /sbin/launchd, is normally reached
-	 * from bsd_ast() the first time the newly-cloned init thread takes an
-	 * AST.  That thread never gets scheduled this early on this board, so
-	 * the trigger never fires and the boot stops here with the root already
-	 * mounted.  Call it directly on this thread instead: load_init_program
-	 * execs launchd, which turns this thread into the init process. */
-	nio_bmark("\nnio: call bsdinit_task directly");
-	bsdinit_task();
+	/* nio: run 605 showed that calling bsdinit_task() on this boot thread
+	 * is wrong: current_proc() is kernproc and current_task() is kernel_task,
+	 * so exec uses the kernel map/task and fails with EFAULT, then the failure
+	 * path trips assert(task != kernel_task) in task_start_halt_locked().
+	 * Since run 598/602 the init thread can be created (post-cloneproc is
+	 * reached), so let the normal bsd_ast() trigger run bsdinit_task() on the
+	 * real init thread, where current_proc/task/map are all correct. */
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: defer bsdinit_task to init thread AST");
 }
 
 #if defined(XNU_OWNER_ROOT_AUDIT) && XNU_OWNER_ROOT_AUDIT
